      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Cell Division – Meaning"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Cell cycle consists of Interphase (G1, S, G2 phases) followed by M-Phase (Mitosis/Meiosis).",
        "Mitosis is an equational division that occurs in somatic cells to produce two genetically identical diploid daughter cells.",
        "Meiosis is a reductional division occurring in germ cells to produce four non-identical haploid gametes.",
        "DNA replication occurs exclusively during the S-phase (Synthesis Phase) of Interphase.",
        "Crossing over and genetic recombination take place during Prophase I (Pachytene stage) of Meiosis."
      ],
      "id": "aj9vw7l"
    },
